result:
### Rationale
I built the library pipeline and ran it on the rented B200. It passes 16/16 on every version and projects to 0.594 on the portal, against 0.304 for the fp32 anchor. That is just under the 0.60 target. The thesis is only partly supported. The GEMMs are not the problem: cuBLASLt costs 5 to 14 µs per GEMM at the S/M shapes, and the fp16 hidden round trip is cheap (H16 is refuted). Each custom launch costs 6 to 17 µs here, not the assumed 2 µs, so the five or six launches put S rows at 35 to 55 µs. The success criteria fail for 7 of the 10 S/M rows and for 32,768,7,7 and the largest shape.

